    "description": "Infirmary, level 3 of 3: L2 plus flourish 3. Over budget: 463 blocks vs 285 (first build 389 vs 235). White plaster ward in a dark oak frame under a spruce gable roof, a red wool cross on white in the front gable: six beds (three on each side, heads to the wall, a window over each), bedside tables, a hearth, herb barrels and shelves, a lean-to herb store; L2 adds the brewing stand and cauldron, candles, lanterns, flower boxes, a door canopy and the banner; L3 a herb garden, herb pots, more banners, a bench and a lantern post. Not yet builder-tested: allium, brewing_stand, brick_stairs, candle, cauldron, cornflower, dandelion, fern, oxeye_daisy, sweet_berry_bush, white_wall_banner. Decoration step adds: banner_pattern, item, potted_plant.",
    "changes": "The red cross now reads as one: red wool on a white wool field in the front gable overhang (QC: the brick cross looked like chimney masonry); L1 gets a bench and a planter by the front, L2 sills under the side and back windows, L3 lanterns on the herb-bed end posts.",
